50
00:05:16,974 --> 00:05:24,004
By customizing prompts, tools, and behaviors, you can build agents that are tailored to your own projects and development workflow.

51
00:05:24,654 --> 00:05:28,868
Alongside agents is Q, Trey's intelligent programming assistant.

52
00:05:29,422 --> 00:05:37,904
Q is designed to make everyday coding faster by providing intelligent code completion, multi-line edits, next edit prediction, edit navigation,

53
00:05:38,064 --> 00:05:41,156
automatic imports, and intelligent renaming across your project.

54
00:05:41,582 --> 00:05:51,524
Instead of simply suggesting the next word, Q often predicts entire blocks of code, helping reduce repetitive typing and keeping you focused on solving problems rather than writing bulletplate.

55
00:05:52,142 --> 00:05:57,904
Trey also supports something called the Model Context Protocol, or MCP.

56
00:05:58,286 --> 00:06:03,748
MCP is an open standard that allows AI models to communicate with external tools and services.

57
00:06:04,206 --> 00:06:13,444
Inside Trey, agents can connect to MCP servers, giving them access to custom APIs, databases, documentation, internal company tools,

58
00:06:13,710 --> 00:06:14,852
and other resources.

59
00:06:15,406 --> 00:06:22,724
As you become more advanced, MCP allows you to extend what your AI agents are capable of far beyond simply generating code.

60
00:06:23,342 --> 00:06:26,276
